+	/*
+	 * A source-root mountpoint is only needed if existing destination mounts
+	 * can be tucked above it.  Allocating it unconditionally also rejects
+	 * moving an otherwise valid bind whose backing inode has been unlinked.
+	 * namespace_sem is held, so the destination cannot change between this
+	 * check and attachment. Shared destinations still need preallocation for
+	 * propagation, and occupied destinations retain all existing checks.
+	 */
+	bool need_root_mountpoint;
+	scoped_guard(mount_locked_reader)
